---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import RatingBadge from '../../components/RatingBadge.astro';
import { destinations, rankForMonth, destMonthUrl, deg, MONTHS } from '../../lib/data';
import { collectionByKey } from '../../lib/collections';

const europe = destinations.filter((d) => d.region === 'Europe');
const europeMonth = collectionByKey.get('europe')!;
const warmest = collectionByKey.get('europe-warm')!;
const top = MONTHS.map((_, m) => rankForMonth(m, europe).slice(0, 5));
const greatCount = MONTHS.map((_, m) => europe.filter((d) => d.months[m].score >= 80).length);

// One line of editorial context per month.
const NOTES = [
  'Cold and dark in the north, but the cheapest month to fly. Winter sun means the Canary Islands, Madeira and Malta; snow means the Alps and Lapland.',
  'Still winter almost everywhere. Ski season peaks, Carnival brings Venice and the Canaries to life, and southern Spain starts to warm up.',
  'Spring arrives in the south: Seville, the Algarve and Sicily are mild and green, while the Alps still have good snow.',
  'Blossom, Easter and long, mild days around the Mediterranean; northern cities are fresh but brightening fast.',
  'One of the best months for almost anywhere: warm in the south, pleasant in the north, and ahead of the summer crowds and prices.',
  'Beach season starts, the Greek islands and Croatia are hot but not yet packed, and Scandinavia has endless daylight.',
  'Peak summer: hot and crowded on the Mediterranean, with heatwaves inland. The best time for Scandinavia, Scotland, Iceland and the Alps.',
  "Europe's busiest holiday month — Italians and French head for the coast. Go north or high into the mountains for comfortable temperatures.",
  'Arguably the best month of all: the sea is at its warmest, the crowds thin out and city breaks are pleasant again.',
  'Warm autumn days in the south and wine harvests everywhere; the north turns cool and colourful.',
  'Quiet, cheap and often grey. The far south (Canaries, Cyprus, Malta) still has sunshine; Christmas markets open at the end of the month.',
  'Christmas markets in Central Europe, skiing from mid-month and the shortest days of the year. Winter sun is limited to the Canaries and Madeira.',
];
---

<Guide slug="best-time-to-visit-europe" photo="cinque-terre">
  <p>
    The short answer: <strong>May, June and September</strong> are the best months to visit most of Europe. They combine warm
    weather with longer days, thinner crowds and lower prices than July and August. But Europe stretches from the Arctic to
    North Africa, so the best time depends on where you go. Below, we rank all {europe.length} European destinations we cover
    for every month, using average temperatures and rainfall from official climate normals.
  </p>

  <h2>Europe by season at a glance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Spring (March–May):</b> best for the Mediterranean, Spain, Portugal and Italy before the heat; tulips in the Netherlands in April; still skiing in the Alps until about Easter.</li>
    <li><b>Summer (June–August):</b> best for Scandinavia, the UK and Ireland, Iceland and the Alps. Very hot and busy in the south, especially in July and August.</li>
    <li><b>Autumn (September–November):</b> September and October are ideal for beaches and city breaks in the south; colours and harvests everywhere; November is quiet and grey.</li>
    <li><b>Winter (December–February):</b> Christmas markets, skiing and the Northern Lights in the north; mild winter sun only in the Canary Islands, Madeira, Cyprus and Malta.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Europe month by month</h2>
  {
    top.map((items, m) => (
      <>
        <h3>{MONTHS[m]}</h3>
        <p>{NOTES[m]} <span class="muted">{greatCount[m]} of {europe.length} destinations rate great.</span></p>
        <ul class="picks">
          {items.map((d) => (
            <li>
              <a href={destMonthUrl(d, m)}>{d.name}</a> <RatingBadge score={d.months[m].score} rating={d.months[m].rating} />
              <span class="muted small">{deg(d.months[m].high)} · {d.months[m].rain} mm</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="small">
          More: <a href={europeMonth.path(m)}>best places to visit in Europe in {MONTHS[m]}</a> ·{' '}
          <a href={warmest.path(m)}>warmest places in Europe in {MONTHS[m]}</a>
        </p>
      </>
    ))
  }

  <h2>By region</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>The Mediterranean</b> (Spain, Italy, Greece, Croatia, Cyprus): May–June and September–October. See <a href="/best-time-to-visit-mediterranean/">the best time to visit the Mediterranean</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Northern Europe and Scandinavia:</b> June–August, when days are longest and warmest. See <a href="/best-time-to-visit-scandinavia/">Scandinavia</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Central and Eastern Europe</b> (Prague, Vienna, Budapest, Kraków): May–June and September, plus December for Christmas markets. See <a href="/best-time-to-visit-central-europe/">Central Europe</a> and <a href="/best-time-to-visit-eastern-europe/">Eastern Europe</a>.</li>
    <li><b>The Alps:</b> late June–September for hiking, December–April for skiing. See <a href="/best-time-to-visit-alps/">the Alps</a>.</li>
    <li><b>The Canary Islands and Madeira:</b> all year, and Europe's best bet for winter sun. See <a href="/best-time-to-visit-canary-islands/">the Canary Islands</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Crowds and prices</h2>
  <p>
    July and August are Europe's peak months: flights, hotels and big sights are at their most expensive, and many locals take
    their own holidays, so some city restaurants close while coasts fill up. Shoulder months — April–May and September–October —
    usually offer the best balance; see our <a href="/guides/shoulder-season/">shoulder-season guide</a>. January to March,
    outside school holidays and ski resorts, is the cheapest time to go, and the
    <a href="/guides/cheapest-months-to-fly-to-europe/">cheapest time to fly to Europe from the US</a>.
  </p>
</Guide>

<style>
  .picks {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .picks li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
